WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
Today will be showing you how to quickly
troubleshoot your production application

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:07.100
using Google Cloud Debugger. The debugger
helps you inspect the call stack

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.639
variables of your application without
stopping or slowing down. First make sure

00:00:11.639 --> 00:00:14.440
the application is up and running.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:20.640
Navigate to source code &gt; debug in the
left nav, then the source code. Set a

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.810
snapshot by clicking in the gutter next
to the line we wish to investigate. Wait

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:32.140
for the request that triggers the snapshot.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:39.070
That was fast! Look at the results
once triggered the snapshot returns 
the call stack and

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.199
local variables without stopping or
slowing down your application. We've

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:48.890
shown you how to troubleshoot your
production application for additional

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:52.160
information take a look at the
documentation and we provide support on

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:52.629
Stackoverflow.

